  "id": "Compound::DB00370 - Gene::154",
  "verbalization": "Mirtazapine is implicated in the regulation of Adrb2 through a series of mechanistic pathways that involve the binding of the drug to Adrb1, which then participates in various receptor activities. The evidence suggests that Mirtazapine interacts with Adrb1, leading to its involvement in the binding of norepinephrine and epinephrine, as well as in beta-adrenergic receptor activity. These interactions ultimately result in the activation of Adrb2. The cumulative scores from the three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Mirtazapine and Adrb2, supported by multiple layers of molecular and functional connections. The mechanism appears to involve the modulation of adrenergic receptor activity, which is a well-documented pathway in the context of drug action. The presence of multiple independent pathways converging on Adrb2 supports the hypothesis that Mirtazapine exerts its effects through a direct interaction with Adrb1, influencing the downstream signaling of Adrb2.",
